    "What is your relationship with mathematics?": "Mathematics has always been a double-edged sword for me. On one hand, I find its logical structure fascinating, especially in economics where it helps me analyze data and solve real-world problems. On the other, my lower secondary education left gaps that still haunt me, making complex topics feel overwhelming. It’s a mix of admiration and frustration.",
    "Do you ever get anxious when thinking about mathematics?": "Yes, often. My neuroticism score reflects this—math triggers anxiety, especially when I’m under pressure or dealing with abstract concepts like calculus. But I’ve learned to break problems into smaller steps, which helps me manage it, though the stress never fully disappears.",
    "Did you ever use AI to support your math learning in the last year? If yes, how was your experience?": "I’ve experimented with AI tools for math, but my low openness to new experiences made adoption difficult. When I did try them, they were helpful for basic algebra, but I preferred human tutors for deeper understanding. The experience was mixed—useful but not transformative.",
